  <h1>Data Deletion Instructions</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: November 21, 2026</p>

  <p>Auto Post does not have a server and does not keep any user data online. All data (login tokens and the
    connected account names) is stored only on the owner's own computer.</p>

  <h2>How to delete your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>In the app:</b> open "Connect accounts" and click "Disconnect" for YouTube, Facebook or TikTok.
      The stored tokens are deleted immediately.</li>
    <li><b>Google / YouTube:</b> remove "Auto Post" at
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Facebook:</b> go to Settings &amp; privacy &gt; Settings &gt; Business integrations, select
      "Auto Post" and click "Remove".</li>
    <li><b>TikTok:</b> go to Settings and privacy &gt; Security &gt; Manage app permissions, select
      "Auto Post" and click "Remove access".</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Request deletion by email</h2>
  <p>If you believe Auto Post holds any data about you, email <a href="mailto:mrkuon12354@gmail.com">mrkuon12354@gmail.com</a> with the subject "Data deletion".
    The request will be handled within 30 days.</p>
</main>
<footer>Auto Post is not affiliated with, endorsed or sponsored by Google, YouTube, Meta, Facebook or TikTok.</footer>
